# OpenSSH allowed_signers file (see ssh-keygen(1) "ALLOWED SIGNERS").
#
# One principal per authorized key, restricted to the domain(s) it may sign
# for via the `namespaces=` option:
#
#   principal-name namespaces="domain-a,domain-b" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# Provisioning (offline, by an operator with access to the corresponding
# private key):
#   1. ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f <key-path> -N ""
#   2. Append a line here: "<principal> namespaces=\"<domain>\" $(cat <key-path>.pub)"
#   3. Have the addition reviewed and committed like any other change to this
#      repository.
#
# No production principals are provisioned yet (WHI-552 ships the signing
# module only; enabling production sends is out of scope for this issue).
